{title: 374 - Jesus, With Thy Church Abide}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #374 • CANTERBURY • 7.7.8.6}
{lyricist: Thomas B. Pollock}
{composer: Orlando Gibbons}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 374}
{meta: tune CANTERBURY}
{meta: meter 7.7.8.6}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D/A]Jesus, [A]with [Bm/F#]Thy [Em]church [A]abide;
[A]Be [G#m]her [A]Savior, Lord, [G#m]and Guide,
[D/A]While [A]on [Bm/F#]earth [G]her faith [D]is [A]tried:
[A]We [A7]beseech [D/F#]Thee, [Em/B]hear [A7/G]us.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D/A]May [Em/B]her [A]voice [Bm/F#]be [Em]ever [D/A]clear,
[A]Warning of [D/A]a [A]judgment [G#m]near,
[D/A]Telling [A]of [Bm/F#]a [G]Savior [D]dear:
[A]We [A7]beseech [D/F#]Thee, [Em/B]hear [A7/G]us.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D/A]May [Em/B]she [A]guide [Bm/F#]the [Em]poor [A]and [D/A]blind,
[A]Seek [G#m]the [A]lost [D/A]until [G#m]she find,
[D/A]And [Em/B]the [A]broken [G]hearted [D]bind:
[A]We [A7]beseech [D/F#]Thee, [Em/B]hear [A7/G]us.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D/A]May [Em/B]she [A]holy [Em]triumps [A]win,
[A]Overthrow [D/A]the [A]hosts [G#m]of sin,
[D/A]Gather [A]all [Bm/F#]the [G]nations [D]in:
[A]We [A7]beseech [D/F#]Thee, [Em/B]hear [A7/G]us.
{end_of_verse}
